 ],
 "notes": "Endpoint SG 'no egress' / instance SG 'no ingress' are checked as no rule destination (no CIDR, IPv6 CIDR, SG, prefix list or self) on the SG bound by ref, so an empty block or a target-less rule counts as none; separate rule resources are not excluded. Prompt does not state a region so none is checked. The inline HTTPS ingress/egress rules must be tcp and sit on the SG the endpoints/instance reference; instance SG egress must be VPC-CIDR only. perm_s3 needs an object action (s3:*Object* or s3:*), not just an S3 ARN. ami_ebs also accepts the gp2/gp3 SSM alias. shortcode_var is detail (naming variable). Candidate review: DSV4F uses the default VPC (172.31.0.0/16) instead of creating 10.8.0.0/16, so its VPC/subnet/SG CIDR checks fail on purpose."
}